From f8c9e2a97efc41a29be8c01095fd744061ff1603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:19:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] docs: drop the Python 3.9 compatibility claims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

85 module docstrings ended with "兼容 Python 3.9+" and 14 test fixtures said
they support 3.9-3.12. Every package requires Python >= 3.12, and the code uses
StrEnum (3.11+) and PEP 604 unions evaluated by Pydantic, so it cannot even be
imported on 3.9. Remove the claims; keep the Pydantic v2 note where it was part
of the same sentence.

CONTRIBUTING asked for Optional[X] / List[X] instead of X | None, which the
enforced ruff UP rules reject. Describe the convention the code follows.
